# ⚡ European Balancing Market Forecasting & Risk Intelligence Platform

## Electricity Balancing Analytics, Forecasting & Risk Intelligence for European Power Markets

## 🌐 Live Demo

The interactive Streamlit dashboard is available here:

👉 https://industry-projects-5mshb3elzypw7kr7ajwtdm.streamlit.app

---

# Project Overview

The **European Balancing Market Forecasting & Risk Intelligence Platform** is an end-to-end energy analytics project developed to analyze electricity balancing markets across major European power systems.

The project demonstrates the complete workflow of an energy analytics platform, including:

- Market data engineering
- Feature engineering
- Electricity balancing analytics
- Renewable generation analysis
- Machine learning forecasting
- Risk intelligence
- Interactive Streamlit dashboard

The objective is to simulate a real-world analytics environment supporting:

- Energy Market Analysts
- Balancing Market Analysts
- Trading Teams
- Risk Management Departments

---

# ⚠️ Demo Repository Notice

This GitHub repository contains the **demo deployment version** of the project.

The original local implementation includes a significantly larger production environment containing:

- Historical ENTSO-E market datasets
- Additional balancing market files
- Intermediate processing outputs
- Forecast artifacts
- Extended forecasting pipelines
- Larger analytical datasets

These files are intentionally excluded from GitHub because they exceed repository size recommendations and are not required for demonstrating the platform architecture.

The current repository includes everything necessary to understand the project design, including:

- Interactive Streamlit dashboard
- Forecasting framework
- Risk analytics modules
- Feature engineering pipeline
- Backtesting framework
- Demo datasets used for deployment
- Complete source code

The demo version reproduces the analytical workflow while using representative sample datasets instead of the complete production environment.

---

# Business Problem

Electricity balancing markets play a critical role in maintaining grid stability by correcting deviations between electricity demand and generation.

Increasing renewable penetration introduces additional uncertainty due to:

- Weather dependency
- Generation volatility
- Forecast errors
- Price fluctuations
- Imbalance exposure

Energy market participants require analytical tools to:

- Forecast system conditions
- Monitor imbalance risk
- Quantify market stress
- Identify operational risks

This project develops a complete analytics platform addressing these challenges.
Increasing renewable penetration introduces additional uncertainty due to:

